  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Keren Eparchy HIV &amp; AIDS Social Support Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The issue of HIV &amp; AIDS is nowadays masked by the news of world economic recession, natural and man made disasters, terrorism, wars, famine, etc., and donor&#x2019;s interest to support HIV &amp; AIDS programmes is reducing.  As a result, PLWHA suffer from lack of attention and care. Therefore, the Catholic Eparchial Secretariat of Keren (CESK) is trying to fill the gap through this project. The aim of the project is to provide preventative and rehabilitative services to 220 PLWHA and 40 orphans living in the Eparchy of Keren. The project will provide counselling and consultation, home-based care, orphan care, social support, micro-credit and health awareness sessions. CESK had been implementing HIV &amp; AIDS activities for more than 10 years. Over a decade of experience has acquainted people with the realities of HIV &amp; AIDS and allowed much needed care and support to be provided to people living with and affected by HIV &amp; AIDS.</narrative>
  </description>
